From 0b0fc97d28a6f43b19f8e69e557f11c586882b72 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: barracuda156 <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 22:00:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 32/70] ppc32: fix the pointer-size assert in
 LoadEntryFromBuiltinIndex

12.4 re-derivation of the 9.4-series patch 0029, identical in content
(TurboAssembler merged into MacroAssembler and the function gained a
target register parameter; static_assert spelling updated).

The function body is already 32-bit-clean through the pointer-size
helper lowering: on ppc32 the SmiValuesAre31Bits() path runs
ShiftLeftU64 -> slwi by (kSystemPointerSizeLog2 - kSmiShift) = 1, which
turns a Smi (index << 1) into index * kSystemPointerSize, and LoadU64
-> lwzx reads the entry from the builtin entry table off kRootRegister.
Only the blanket static_assert(kSystemPointerSize == 8) was wrong;
split it per-arch exactly as the validated 8.4/9.4 series did.

A sweep of all ppc backend/masm/builtins dirs confirms this is still
the only blanket pointer-size assert at 12.4.
---
 v8/src/codegen/ppc/macro-assembler-ppc.cc | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/v8/src/codegen/ppc/macro-assembler-ppc.cc b/v8/src/codegen/ppc/macro-assembler-ppc.cc
index 8ae0b66..fd3bb3c 100644
--- a/v8/src/codegen/ppc/macro-assembler-ppc.cc
+++ b/v8/src/codegen/ppc/macro-assembler-ppc.cc
@@ -5305,7 +5305,11 @@ void MacroAssembler::JumpIfUnsignedLessThan(Register x, int32_t y,
 
 void MacroAssembler::LoadEntryFromBuiltinIndex(Register builtin_index,
                                                Register target) {
+#if V8_TARGET_ARCH_PPC64
   static_assert(kSystemPointerSize == 8);
+#else
+  static_assert(kSystemPointerSize == 4);
+#endif
   static_assert(kSmiTagSize == 1);
   static_assert(kSmiTag == 0);
 
